    "result_text": "The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the class behind `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Added a blocklist constant** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:82`):\n   ```java\n   private static final Set<String> DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS =\n       Set.of(\"mailinator.com\", \"tempmail.com\", \"guerrillamail.com\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Extended `normalizeEmail`** to extract the domain (after `@`, compared case-insensitively) and throw `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"email\"))` when it's on the blocklist. That existing exception is already mapped to **400 Bad Request** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\nI placed the check inside `normalizeEmail`, which is called from both the create and update paths, so it's consistently enforced. It runs after the existing syntactic/`null` checks, keeping email optional (a `null` email is still accepted) while rejecting present disposable-domain addresses.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) and the full suite pass.",
